    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change lands cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The national-length rule goes into `OwnerTelephones.toE164`, which is explicitly the \"single source of truth\" for the E.164 rule and is already shared by both `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` and (per its docstring) the validation path. Adding the new constraint here means both consumers inherit it for free \u2014 no duplication.\n- **No catch-all growth.** The new logic is a small, cohesive addition to an already-focused helper, not bolted onto `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` or the exception class.\n- **Data-driven and extensible.** The `NATIONAL_DIGITS` map with a documented longest-prefix ordering is the natural way to express \"country code \u2192 required national length,\" and extending to more countries is a one-line map entry rather than new branching.\n- **Docs kept coherent.** The Javadoc on `OwnerTelephones`, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, and `InvalidTelephoneException`, plus the thrown message, were all updated in step with the behavior, preserving the existing cross-reference style between these classes.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this a natural extension of the existing telephone-rule design.",
